  "$comment": "EnRuPackPlan.md §1.3/§6 EN-14: the wiring ExerciseGenerator reads for every one of lang/en/curriculum.json's 16 skills, mirroring lang/pl/exercise-recipes.json's own convention exactly — every string outside a construction/feature/case identifier is an opaque exerciseCopy/exercisePattern KEY (resolved through pairs/en-ru/pair.json, EN-17), never English or Russian text written here. `defaultOwnerLexeme`/`verbLexeme` are pl's own convention, reused unchanged. `constantSlots` is new (EnRuPackPlan.md §5 gap A): pack-constant lexical slots beyond `owner`/`verb` that ExerciseGenerator now fills conditionally on a phrase's own resolved Case/Polarity/Tense/Aspect/Mood — `prep` (the role preposition, absent for Subj/Obj), `aux`/`neg` (do-support, present only for Polarity=Neg or Mood=YesNoQ; `will`/`be` for the periphrastic Tense=Fut/Aspect=Continuous), and `subject` (mood.question's fixed \"you\", unconditional — every other construction here simply has no `subject` slot to fill). Skill ids are `en:`-namespaced (curriculum.json, EN-12) unlike pl's bare ids, so both packs' recipes never collide even though the underlying construction ids are shared.",
  "$comment_verbLexeme": "\"walk\" (EnRuPackPlan.md §1.3: a neutral, fully regular verb, deliberately not \"go\") is the lexicalSlots[\"verb\"] value core.verb.tense/core.sentence.polarity/core.sentence.mood realize through ConstructionRealizer — the only 7 skills (verb.presentSimple/pastSimple/futureSimple/presentContinuous, polarity.present/past, mood.question) whose own construction actually needs a realized verb form. Every other skill's copy pattern bakes its own fixed verb (\"see\"/\"saw\"/\"did not see\") directly as pack-authored text, exactly like pl's \"seenAcc\"/\"chainPast\" patterns — those skills drill a noun-phrase transformation, not verb conjugation, so the verb they show is presentation, not `:core-engine` realization.",
  "defaultOwnerLexeme": "my",
  "verbLexeme": "walk",
  "constantSlots": [
    { "slot": "prep", "lexeme": "role", "whenFeature": "Case", "whenValues": ["In", "With", "To", "About", "Of"] },
    { "slot": "aux", "lexeme": "do", "whenFeature": "Polarity", "whenValues": ["Neg"] },
    { "slot": "neg", "lexeme": "not", "whenFeature": "Polarity", "whenValues": ["Neg"] },
    { "slot": "aux", "lexeme": "will", "whenFeature": "Tense", "whenValues": ["Fut"] },
    { "slot": "aux", "lexeme": "be", "whenFeature": "Aspect", "whenValues": ["Continuous"] },
    { "slot": "aux", "lexeme": "do", "whenFeature": "Mood", "whenValues": ["YesNoQ"] },
    { "slot": "subject", "lexeme": "you" }
  ],
